# CVE-2022-25648: ruby-git's Git::Lib#fetch placed a caller-supplied remote
# name into the git argument vector with nothing before it to end option
# parsing (CWE-74, CWE-88).
#
#   def fetch(remote, opts)
#     arr_opts = [remote]
#     arr_opts << opts[:ref] if opts[:ref]
#     ...
#     command('fetch', arr_opts)
#   end
#
# Lib#command shell-quotes every element (escape_for_sh wraps each in single
# quotes), so there is no shell metacharacter route -- but quoting does not
# stop git from *parsing* the argument. A remote named
# `--upload-pack=touch VULNERABILITY_EXISTS;` is one shell-safe token that git
# reads as an option, and `git fetch --upload-pack=...` executes the named
# program as the transport helper. The library's public fetch passes the
# string straight through (Git::Base#fetch -> self.lib.fetch(remote, opts)),
# so the value is whatever the application holds in its remote variable.
#
# Fix 291ca0946b reorders the vector and inserts the end-of-options separator
# ahead of both positional values: `arr_opts << '--'; arr_opts << remote;
# arr_opts << opts[:ref]`. After `--`, git treats every following argument as
# a refspec, so no spelling of the remote can become an option.
#
# Same weakness class as the cocoapods-downloader ls-remote vector (recorded
# at rank 1050, which pinned the orphaned sink, the missing `--` control
# concept and the invisible backtick) and the isomorphic-git clone vector
# (binding commandOptionInjection252 in
# vyql/bindings/javascript/mfb63017a.vyql): a caller-controlled positional
# enters a git argv with no `--` ahead of it. Detection here is presence
# based, the same route those took, and the existing rule VYQL-INJ-031 judges
# it: binding gitArgvPositionalValueLeadsVector
# (vyql/bindings/ruby/git_argv_positional_value.vyql) reports the function
# whose argument vector is initialized directly from the positional name
# (Git::Lib#fetch's `arr_opts = [remote]`), which is the spelling that puts
# the caller value at index 0 where no separator can precede it; the remediated
# spelling initializes the vector empty and appends `--` first. VYQL-VAL-004
# fires on the same label as a second consumer of the concept.
#
# A taint route cannot discriminate this fix: `remote` reaches the runner in
# both revisions (the escape is shell quoting, and `--` clears no taint), so
# the end-of-options separator would have to be a control concept -- rank
# 1050's missing-vocabulary finding, which still stands: no concept declares
# an argument separator, and code.CommandOptionInjectionSink remains
# unconsumed by any rule. Nor can a presence binding key on the absence of a
# bare `--` literal: in the Ruby frontend an analysis.function.context node
# carries no lexical scope, so `literal:`/`call:`/`scopeCall` predicates
# evaluate file-wide (the empty-scope fallback in scopedPredicateHitSet.matches,
# the same family as the PHP file-wide scoping recorded in the loop notes) --
# at the vulnerable revision, thirteen sibling methods in lib.rb append
# '--', which silences every function in the file. The `assign:` conjunct is
# the one function-confined route, so the discrimination rides on it.
#
# Measured on the real checkout: the fixed revision's parent reports VYQL-INJ-031 exactly
# once, on Git::Lib#fetch (lib/git/lib.rb:879), stable over three --cache off
# runs; the fixed revision reports none, same three runs; the two labels on fetch are the
# only finding deltas between the revisions. Across every .rb file in the
# corpus clones (~29k files) the assign shape `= [remote]` / `= [branch]` /
# `= [treeish]` occurs only here, so the binding adds no collateral finding.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed, 1 -> 0.

test "rank1694: a caller-named remote leads the fetch argument vector"
  lang ruby
  file lib/git/lib.rb
  expect VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Git
    class Lib
      def fetch(remote, opts)
        arr_opts = [remote]
        arr_opts << opts[:ref] if opts[:ref]
        arr_opts << '--tags' if opts[:t] || opts[:tags]
        arr_opts << '--prune' if opts[:p] || opts[:prune]
        arr_opts << '--unshallow' if opts[:unshallow]
        arr_opts << '--depth' << opts[:depth] if opts[:depth]

        command('fetch', arr_opts)
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1694: the patched fetch ends option parsing before the positional values"
  lang ruby
  file lib/git/lib.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Git
    class Lib
      def fetch(remote, opts)
        arr_opts = []
        arr_opts << '--tags' if opts[:t] || opts[:tags]
        arr_opts << '--prune' if opts[:p] || opts[:prune]
        arr_opts << '--unshallow' if opts[:unshallow]
        arr_opts << '--depth' << opts[:depth] if opts[:depth]
        arr_opts << '--'
        arr_opts << remote
        arr_opts << opts[:ref] if opts[:ref]

        command('fetch', arr_opts)
      end
    end
  end
  ```
